1
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:48,222
They're taking adventure to new lengths.

2
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:30,444
Tangled is a animation, family, adventure film directed by Byron Howard.

3
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:12,666
Feisty teenager Rapunzel, who has long and magical hair, wants to go and see sky lanterns on her
eighteenth birthday, but she's bound to a tower by her overprotective mother.

4
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:54,888
She strikes a deal with Flynn Rider, a charming wanted thief,
and the duo set off on an action-packed escapade.

5
00:18:31,111 --> 00:18:37,111
Rapunzel (voice), played by Mandy Moore.

6
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:19,333
Flynn Rider (voice), played by Zachary Levi.

7
00:25:55,555 --> 00:26:01,555
Mother Gothel (voice), played by Donna Murphy.

8
00:29:37,777 --> 00:29:43,777
Stabbington Brother (voice), played by Ron Perlman.

9
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Captain of the Guard (voice), played by M.C. Gainey.

10
00:37:02,222 --> 00:37:08,222
Big Nose Thug (voice), played by Jeffrey Tambor.

11
00:40:44,444 --> 00:40:50,444
Tangled is a 2010 American animated musical fantasy comedy film loosely based on the
German fairy tale "Rapunzel", and produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios.

12
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:32,666
Directed by Nathan Greno and Byron Howard, and written by Dan Fogelman,
it stars Mandy Moore, Zachary Levi, and Donna Murphy.

13
00:48:08,888 --> 00:48:14,888
The film tells the story of Rapunzel, a young princess with magical
long blonde hair who tries to leave her secret tower.

14
00:51:51,111 --> 00:51:57,111
She accepts the aid of an intruder, the outlaw Flynn Rider, to take
her out into the world which she has never seen.

15
00:55:33,333 --> 00:55:39,333
Originally conceived and proposed by Disney animator Glen Keane in 2001, Tangled spent six years in production at a cost that has been estimated at $260
million, which, if accurate, would make it the most expensive animated feature film ever made and one of the most expensive films of all time.

16
00:59:15,555 --> 00:59:21,555
The film employed a unique artistic style by blending together features of computer-generated imagery (CGI) and
traditional animation while using non-photorealistic rendering to create the impression of a painting.

17
01:02:57,777 --> 01:03:03,777
Composer Alan Menken, who had collaborated on prior Disney animated features, returned to
score Tangled, and also wrote the film's songs with lyricist Glenn Slater.

18
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
Before the film's release, its title was changed from Rapunzel to
Tangled, reportedly to market the film gender-neutrally.

19
01:10:22,222 --> 01:10:28,222
Tangled premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Los Angeles on November 14,
2010, and was released on November 24 by Walt Disney Pictures.

20
01:14:04,444 --> 01:14:10,444
The film earned $592 million and became the
eighth-highest-grossing film of 2010.

21
01:17:46,666 --> 01:17:52,666
Tangled received positive reviews from critics, with particular praise for the animation, and was
nominated for several awards, including Best Original Song at the 83rd Academy Awards.

22
01:21:28,888 --> 01:21:34,888
It was Richard Kiel's last film role before he died in 2014.

23
01:25:11,111 --> 01:25:17,111
Tangled spawned a franchise, including a short film, Tangled Ever After (2012), a video
game, a stage musical, and a television series which premiered in 2017.

24
01:28:53,333 --> 01:28:59,333
A live-action adaptation is in development.

25
01:32:35,555 --> 01:32:41,555
The film explores themes of princess, magic, hostage, fairy tale, horse.

26
01:36:17,777 --> 01:36:23,777
The tone is uplifting.
